-- 102: Plains / South-Central fishing rules (US plan step 4): South Dakota, North Dakota, Oklahoma, Arkansas, Kentucky, Tennessee, West Virginia
-- Checked 2026-10-22 on each state's own pages (links in source_url): South Dakota 2026 Fishing Handbook (statewide harvest and length limits, page 18);
-- North Dakota Fishing Guide 2026-28 (in effect April 1, 2026 – March 31, 2028; statewide limits page 10, fish size restrictions page 12);
-- Oklahoma ODWC "Statewide Daily & Size Limits" page; Arkansas 2026-27 Fishing Guidebook (the PDF linked from AGFC's guidebooks page; rules from July 1, 2026);
-- Kentucky Fishing & Boating Guide March 2026 – February 2027 (updated September 2026), statewide size and daily limits table;
-- Tennessee TWRA "Statewide Regulations and Creel and Length Limits" page (2026-27 rules, in effect Aug 1, 2026); West Virginia 2026 Fishing Regulations Summary (page 1 table).
-- A state rule is a normal fish_rules row whose `regions` holds the 2-letter state code. Needs setup/94 first (its check already allows these codes).
-- Where a rule changes by season, zone or water the app can only show one number, so the STRICTER one is the size / bag and the note has the rest.
-- NOT added: Kansas (ksoutdoors.gov blocks every download, HTTP 403) and Nebraska (the 2026 guide is only page pictures in a flipbook): no rows, the app says
-- "We don't have Kansas / Nebraska rules yet" until Richard gives the guides as PDFs. West Virginia northern pike, blue and flathead catfish (the PDF table's columns
-- come out scrambled there), Kentucky bluegill (not in the table), paddlefish outside Tennessee, Oklahoma trout (separate trout page not read).
-- Insert only; no delete / drop.

insert into fish_rules (species, match, regions, min_in, max_in, measure, one_over, bag, release_only, closed, open_only, note, source_url, verified_on, active) values
